# K5.3: a reader that copies a payload word from a new write must see that
# write's odd head when it re-loads head after the copy.
#
# x = head (published 2, writer takes it odd to 3), d = payload word. The
# writer fences between its odd head and its payload store; the reader
# fences between its payload load and its head re-load. Accepting r1=1 with
# an unchanged head (r2=2) is exactly a torn row.

AetherSeqlockPayloadRecheck

{
  x=2; d=0;
}

P0          | P1          ;
wrlx x 3    | racq r0 x   ;
fence.rel   | rrlx r1 d   ;
wrlx d 1    | fence.acq   ;
wrel x 4    | racq r2 x   ;

exists (P1:r0=2 /\ P1:r1=1 /\ P1:r2=2)
